# Every entry here corresponds to something this repository actually generates.
# It is deliberately not the stock GitHub Node/Rust template: a list naming
# Gatsby, Bower and DynamoDB tells a reader nothing about what this project
# builds, and buries the handful of entries that matter.

# ── Rust ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No leading slash: `cargo fuzz` puts its own build tree at compiler/fuzz/target.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# cargo-mutants working tree
**/mutants.out*/

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
# `npm pack` / `pnpm pack` output. Verifying a tarball is part of releasing, so
# these turn up in the tree regularly.
*.tgz

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every package emits to dist/, and `slurp build` defaults to it. Nothing under
# any dist/ is ever committed.
dist/

# `vsce package` writes the VSIX beside the manifest rather than into dist/.
*.vsix
coverage/

# `compiler-wasm/pkg/` is the wasm-pack artifact. It is ignored by its OWN
# .gitignore rather than an entry here, because npm applies these rules per
# directory and that package needs the file beside it. See
# compiler-wasm/.npmignore for what that interaction cost us once.

# ── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Editors and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode-test/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Maintainer-only, deliberately not published ──────────────────────────────
RELEASING.md
